  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of winterization assistance for the most vulnerable people in NW Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">**Mercy-USA for Aid and Development in this project will support the most vulnerable people in NW Syria with Cash for winter (150 USD) for each HH one-off during October, November, and December in Idleb, Maaret Tamsrin, Darkosh and Jandairis sub-districts 

Total number of beneficiaries who will be targeted will be 11,000 HH - 59,031 individuals (Men 12,208-  Women 14,075- Boys 17,082- Girls 15,666) by using cash modality for implementation.
The targeted beneficiaries will be Mercy-USA beneficiaries from ongoing or completed projects with other humanitarian assistance such as food assistance. Moreover,  Mercy-USA will register new beneficiaries in the same locations as backup list in case of any update in the beneficiaries lists to reach the targeted caseload.
 The selection criteria for beneficiaries will be based on their existence in Mercy-USA beneficiaries list for other projects while adding new beneficiaries will be based on set of vulnerability criteria to choose the most vulnerable people. 

**Accountability to Affected population (AAP) will be given high priority in this project by communications and sharing information with beneficiaries during all project phases, as well as using complaints and feedback mechanism which is accessible to all beneficiaries especially the most vulnerable such as persons with disabilities, the elderly, women and girls, thus taking corrective actions 
based on need.

** Furthermore, MEAL plan will be for all project stages such as verification of vulnerability assessment, distribution monitoring, PDM, with using different MEAL tools.</narrative>
  </description>
